In a Databricks Data Engineering project, the overall tasks usually cover data ingestion, transformation, storage, orchestration, data quality, testing, and deployment. Below is a typical end-to-end project workflow and the tasks a Data Engineer performs.
Databricks Project – Overall Tasks
Modern Data Engineering Architecture: A Comprehensive Framework | Sai Prasad posted on the topic | LinkedIn
1. Requirement Analysis and Source Identification
Understand business requirements and reporting needs.
Identify source systems: SQL databases, APIs, CSV, JSON, Parquet, and cloud storage.
Define data volume, refresh frequency, and target tables.
Document source-to-target mappings.
End-to-End Data Warehouse Pipeline on Azure: From Raw CSVs to Power BI Dashboards

2. Data Ingestion — Bronze Layer
Connect Databricks to source systems.
Ingest batch or streaming data.
Load raw data into Delta tables or cloud storage.
Implement incremental loading and CDC where required.
Capture ingestion timestamps and source metadata.
HOW TO: Use Databricks Assistant for Data Analysis
  
3. Data Transformation — Silver Layer
Clean and standardize raw data using PySpark or SQL.
Handle null values, duplicates, and invalid records.
Apply business rules and data type conversions.
Join multiple source tables.
Implement Slowly Changing Dimensions (SCD Type 1/2), if required.
Building a Unified Data Layer for Analytics and AI Integration | by Tanmay Unhale | Medium
  
4. Business Data Modeling — Gold Layer
Create business-ready Delta tables.
Build fact and dimension tables.
Calculate KPIs, aggregations, and business metrics.
Prepare data for Power BI, Tableau, or downstream applications.
Optimize tables and queries for performance.
Databricks Data Intelligence Platform | Dataprix
  
5. Workflow Orchestration
Create Databricks Jobs or Lakeflow Jobs.
Schedule daily, hourly, or event-driven pipelines.
Configure task dependencies and parameters.
Set retries, timeouts, and failure notifications.
Monitor pipeline execution and resolve failures.
Best Practices and Recommendations for Monitoring with DLT on Databricks
  
6. Data Quality and Testing
Validate source and target record counts.
Check nulls, duplicates, schema, and business rules.
Perform unit, integration, and regression testing.
Reconcile transformed data with source data.
Fix defects and document test results.
Unity Catalog Governance Accelerator | Dhristhi
  
7. Security and Governance
Configure Unity Catalog catalogs, schemas, and tables.
Manage access permissions and service principals.
Configure secrets and secure data connections.
Review lineage, auditing, and sensitive-data access.
